ning, the Shieldguard Leaders don heavier protective armor and cover for their comrades by drawing fire from enemies while present on the battlefield.","abilities":["More likely to be targeted by attacks."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":true,"moveSpeed":0.7,"stats":{"hp":25000,"atk":800,"def":2200,"res":60,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":3.8}},"v_t_e":{"slug":"v_t_e","name":"V.T.E.","icon":"/enemies-icons/V.T.E..webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":null,"damageType":["Arts"],"flavourText":"Cutting-edge tactical equipment designed by Rhodes Island's Engineering Department specifically for this round of Vector Breakout training.\nWhile manifesting your emotions takes a toll, it offers strength in equal measure.","abilities":["More likely to be attacked. When attacked, inflicts a certain amount of True damage on surrounding allied units.","Continuously stuns surrounding allies.","Disappears when touched by another enemy, granting that enemy bonus Max HP and ATK. When that enemy is defeated, a <V.T.E.> is created where they fall.","Leaves a Matrix on the field when destroyed. Allies within the Matrix gain bonus Max HP and ATK, and take less Physical and Arts damage.","Self-destructs after being on the field for some time, dealing Arts damage over a wide area."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":1,"stats":{"hp":20000,"atk":100,"def":1000,"res":20,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":1}},"arc_frontliner_leader":{"slug":"arc_frontliner_leader","name":"Arc Frontliner Leader","icon":"/enemies-icons/Arc Frontliner Leader.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Arts"],"flavourText":"Deadly soldiers from an experimental unit outfitted with highly lethal cutting-edge equipment. A formidable foe even when their gear's weaknesses have been revealed.","abilities":["Loses HP proportional to distance moved when shifted"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":true,"moveSpeed":0.75,"stats":{"hp":52000,"atk":1250,"def":1250,"res":60,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":3}},"traffic_tower_prototype":{"slug":"traffic_tower_prototype","name":"'Traffic Tower' Prototype","icon":"/enemies-icons/'Traffic Tower' Prototype.webp","rank":"Elite","race":"Machina","movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"A robot primarily developed by Volvort Kochinski, the crystallization of cutting-edge advances in every field. If they could lower the cost of production to make it feasible for mass-production, perhaps it could even change the nature of warfare.","abilities":["Can only be blocked by units with at least 4 Block","DEF and RES is reduced whenever damage is taken","When destroyed, ejects a <'Traffic Officer Captain'> and self-destructs, dealing physical damage to nearby units"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":true,"moveSpeed":0.8,"stats":{"hp":60000,"atk":1500,"def":9600,"res":90,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":5}},"blade_helmet_knightclub_elite":{"slug":"blade_helmet_knightclub_elite","name":"Blade Helmet Knightclub Elite","icon":"/enemies-icons/Blade Helmet Knightclub Elite.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Arts"],"flavourText":"A regular knight from the Blade Helmet Knightclub. This order of young competition knights chose the name of the ancient heroes of Kazimierz. In fact, they exhibit only arrogance and complacency from that extinct lineage. They are good at picking fights and don't go down easily.","abilities":["Significantly decreases ATK of the unit with the highest ATK for a period of time","Rebirth"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":true,"moveSpeed":0.75,"stats":{"hp":30000,"atk":1000,"def":700,"res":50,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":2.5}},"greater_armored_burdenbeast":{"slug":"greater_armored_burdenbeast","name":"Greater Armored Burdenbeast","icon":"/enemies-icons/Greater Armored Burdenbeast.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Slow, docile, and even larger, these burdenbeasts obediently undergo rigorous training to perform tasks that go against their nature.","abilities":["Will be tripped by a Stabilizer Chain, stunning itself and dealing Physical damage to nearby enemies."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":true,"moveSpeed":0.6,"stats":{"hp":180000,"atk":2800,"def":50,"res":50,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5}},"rosmontiss_drone":{"slug":"rosmontiss_drone","name":"Rosmontis's Drone","icon":"/enemies-icons/Rosmontis's Drone.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Flying","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"A cutting-edge drone designed by Rhodes Island's Engineering Department specifically for this round of Vector Breakout training training.\nRosmontis loves its color.","abilities":["Flying unit.","Can only be attacked while inside a Matrix.","Attacks deal AoE damage.","After two attacks, the next attack stuns all targets.","When defeated, leaves behind Supplies that will activate when Rosmontis, Simulated Sentry triggers [Cognitive Collapse]. Upon activation, allied units in a wide area will take reduced Physical and Arts damage."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.4,"stats":{"hp":10000,"atk":700,"def":550,"res":40,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":5}},"rosmontis_simulated_sentry":{"slug":"rosmontis_simulated_sentry","name":"Rosmontis, Simulated Sentry","icon":"/enemies-icons/Rosmontis, Simulated Sentry.webp","rank":"Boss","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee and Ranged","damageType":["Physical","Arts"],"flavourText":"A Breakthrough Trainer simulating Rosmontis at the peak of her combat prowess.\nAs she gazes at the 'walking arsenal' brought to life from data, her memories are finally liberated. Braver and more determined, she now yearns to fight alongside her companions.","abilities":["[Mind Matrix] Takes less Physical and Arts damage. Loses this effect when the V.T.E. on the field is destroyed and cannot attack until the V.T.E. is re-obtained.","First Form","[Fling] Hurls a <V.T.E.> at an allied unit regardless of distance, dealing 3 instances of Physical damage to the target when it lands (The second and third instances are aftershocks, dealing half damage). Stunned targets are instantly defeated.","[Retrieve] Clears all Matrices on the field and retrieves all Tactical Equipment.","[Impulse Inhibition] Initiates revival when HP reaches 0, periodically dealing Arts damage over a wide area around her every few seconds during the process.","Second Form","[Amplified Fling] Hurls a second <V.T.E.> a few seconds after the first. Stunned targets are instantly defeated.","[Memory Loss] Loses a certain amount of HP with every attack and deals Arts damage over a wide area around her.","[Cognitive Collapse] Once HP drops below 50%, flies into the air and switches to ranged attacks. Increases ATK, no longer uses [Fling], and gains the following abilities:","Attacks stun the target for an extended period. [Mind Matrix] effect no longer expires and reduces damage taken even further. [Memory Loss] damage dealt and HP loss are both increased. When attacked, deals a certain amount of True damage to surrounding allies."],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.4,"stats":{"hp":50000,"atk":2000,"def":1000,"res":50,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":4}}},"dropIcons":{"act1vecb_milestone_point":"/item-icons/attainment_point.png"},"previewFile":"vec-08_